## Provenance note (important)

This project is an **independent implementation**. It was *not* derived from,
forked from, or copied from any GPL-licensed project.

The open-source project **QuietInbox** (<https://gitlab.com/aa22396584/quietinbox>,
GPL-3.0-or-later) was consulted as a **product reference** only — for the general
idea of storing encrypted copies of messaging notifications locally, and for the
use of a source allowlist. No source code, resource, layout, string, or asset
from QuietInbox (or from any other GPL project) was copied into this codebase.

Concretely:

- The package name is `tw.personal.privateinbox`, not QuietInbox's.
- The class names, file layout, database schema, UI layout, colour palette,
  notification parsing logic, diagnostics model and test suite in this repository
  were written for this project.
- The only third-party runtime dependency is `androidx.activity` (Apache-2.0);
  test-only dependencies are `junit` (EPL-1.0) and `androidx.test.*` (Apache-2.0).
- `grep -rniE "quietinbox|aa22396584|ImL1s"` over `app/` and `scripts/` returns
  no matches.

Because no GPL code was incorporated, the MIT terms above apply to this codebase
in full. If GPL-derived code were ever added in the future, this file would
have to be revisited and the corresponding obligations satisfied.
